menu "GBX display"

config GBX_DISPLAY_ACCEL
    bool "Use the PPA / DMA2D presentation backend"
    depends on SOC_PPA_SUPPORTED && SOC_DMA2D_SUPPORTED
    default n
    help
        Select one presentation implementation at build time. The CPU
        implementation is not linked when this is enabled. The shared
        sdkconfig.defaults.<target> file supplies each SoC's display policy.
        LVGL's draw unit is configured separately with LV_USE_PPA.

config GBX_DISPLAY_LOCK_GAME_DRAW
    bool "Keep LVGL from drawing while a game frame is drawn"
    default n
    help
        The present task holds the LVGL lock while it draws a game frame,
        as it does while it copies the UI. An RGB panel's DMA reads the
        frame buffer from PSRAM while the panel scans out; on the
        ESP32-S31 it underran, and the picture shifted, when LVGL drew
        while the PPA drew a game frame. LVGL's changes then show after
        the frame.

config GBX_LVGL_PPA_MIN_PIXELS
    int "Minimum clipped area for the LVGL PPA draw unit"
    depends on LV_USE_PPA
    range 0 16777216
    default 4096
    help
        Smaller draws stay with LVGL's software renderer. This includes
        neither the game scaling choice nor the presentation backend.
        Zero permits all operations supported by the pinned LVGL backend.

endmenu

menu "GBX JIT"

config GBX_JIT_CODE_PSRAM
    bool "Run all generated code from PSRAM"
    depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32P4 && SPIRAM
    default n
    help
        Allocate the JIT code pool and its shared code in PSRAM instead of
        internal RAM, so that every generated block runs from PSRAM through
        the caches. The internal RAM this frees can hold a larger L2 cache
        (CACHE_L2_CACHE_SIZE).

endmenu
